message: "If you use quantum-cortex, its continuity benchmarks, or any derivative work, please cite it as below and retain the NOTICE file (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(d))."
title: "quantum-cortex: an open language model built to measure continuity"
abstract: "A from-scratch, byte-level language model whose cognitive concepts (expert zones, associative memory, an oracle channel, typed decode contracts) live in the weights and the decode loop, built to measure one capability: continuity, as a triad of episodic persistence (the H.M. protocol), adaptive revision (oracle shift) and non regeneration (the reference ratio). Independent member of the Quantum Meridian ecosystem."
